{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1462017-conflict-dilemma","id":1462017,"title":"Conflict dilemma","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-29T14:45:52-07:00","id":1462017,"title":"Conflict dilemma","content":"Long story short:<br /> We are closing our long-time chronicle.<br /> <br /> There will be an escalation against 2 packs of nomad veterans fire touched from Santa Fe, they are leading a crusade in the pack's territory and on other urdaga territories.<br /> There will be blood, revenge, and at the end, open war. There is a pack of Predator Kings (local, but outside the city, Dodge City) that will notice about what the Izidakh are doing: homicide, rape, fake promises and betrayal of pacts with the local forsaken and pure (pure that don't want to join the crusade, only Fire Touched are present).<br /> <br /> <br /> How much '''realistic'' would be to see the Predator Kings hunting down those 2 packs, indirectly, because they are disohonring the hunt, even if against the forsaken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:17:08-07:00","id":1462036,"title":"","content":"Well, there is no such thing as real world Predator Kings, so the word would be &quot;believable&quot; instead of &quot;realistic.&quot; I say that not to nitpick but because I think it simplifies the answer: can you picture a pack of Predator Kings taking things in this way? Yeah, I can picture it. The tribes aren't monoliths, after all; one territory's Predator Kings won't necessarily agree with another's.<br /> <br /> The other relevant question: does it sound interesting and fun as a story turn? To me it does. Big, messy and complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:58:36-07:00","id":1462046,"title":"","content":"I'm more curious how packs with a solid tie to a tribe that predicates a lot on the value of truth and honesty ended up in this scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-29-2021, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T19:53:28-07:00","id":1462067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1462017-conflict-dilemma#post1462017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much '''realistic'' would be to see the Predator Kings hunting down those 2 packs, indirectly, because they are disohonring the hunt, even if against the forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's easy to justify, especially if the Fire-Touched have been dishonoring the hunt, which it seems like they may be with their actions. It gets easier if you have things like the Predator Kings not having a lot of prey, maybe their pack somehow being personally insulted by the Fire-Touched or wanting something they have. Or the opposite, maybe they're just so into the hunt that they don't care what your association is, like Zud'nalu from Shunned by the Moon who's begun to see his fellow tribemates as prey.<br /> <br /> It makes me think of the Brethren War from first edition, where after a while both sides, the Pure and the Forsaken, would fall to infighting (and then enemies) after getting so arrogant and at ease with throwing their weight around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T22:38:01-07:00","id":1462077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1462017-conflict-dilemma?p=1462046#post1462046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more curious how packs with a solid tie to a tribe that predicates a lot on the value of truth and honesty ended up in this scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>During this chronicle I wanted to face a lot of things. From personal emotive crisis that can comes from great trauma and how much the characters can change ,as a moon and werewolf methaphore, with sense of revenge vs sense of honor.<br /> <br /> The main antagonist here is Crucible and also Devil's Dauguter from Pure first edition ( converte 2 ed). Btw, I added some very tragic stuff on Crucible background , involving religious faith and very bad sexual trauma. To answer your question : charismaric figure. Crucible is extremely charismatic but his mind, in truth , was crushed by Gurim ur visions and various action during the Brethren wars, that left his mind unstable, including personal losses. After the local forsaken will not submit to his request of conversion, he will act in order to purify them from their sins galvanizing local pure with his gifts (he is the strongest and smartest fire touched here and he is very intimidating).<br /> <br /> A mixed local pack of pure which is the &quot;healthy&quot; rival of the characters will have a shocking scene where they will refuse to help the massacre out of honor and will kill some forsaken-converted pure trying to burn the characters as initiation rite to submit to crucible. Then, the Predator Kings will enter the hunt, an outsider pack of veterans with a couple of youngsters in the mentioned pack. The character will face the dilemma about trusting the pure and how much, and how to deal with a possible pact of honor with them.<br /> <br /> Those things are all major chronicle stuff which will end the chronicle (for now) and involve all the forsaken and pure communities alike , with enormous repercussions, escalations and great losses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 09-30-2021, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}